From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] include: linux/types.h: add __s128 and __u128

The bundled linux/types.h shadows the sysroot copy, and since Linux 7.3
the arm64 UAPI headers use __u128 in asm/sigcontext.h and asm/ptrace.h,
so building against current headers fails:

  asm/sigcontext.h:81:9: error: unknown type name '__u128'

Add the 128-bit types as the kernel defines them.

Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/types.h	2026-09-26 13:59:58.360134955 +0000
+++ b/include/linux/types.h	2026-09-26 13:59:58.373134973 +0000
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <asm/posix_types.h>
 
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
 #define __bitwise__
 #define __bitwise __bitwise__
 
